IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 11 Division 2 (foreign companies), ss 365 to 367: the scope of the Division,
-- its own definitions, and the power to hold immovable property. Part sgg, layer 1.
-- (Part 11 Division 1 is shown repealed; the later sections of Division 2 are in sgg-lodging.l4 and the modules after it.)
--
-- Every answer is a MAYBE BOOLEAN unless it says otherwise (the rule of 2026-10-29, as the keel reads it):
--   JUST TRUE   the section's own test is met on the facts given;
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no to this case in its own words (each such branch is tagged FALSE-kind and quotes the words);
--   NOTHING     the text does not say (each such branch is tagged NOTHING-kind and says why).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- THE TWO TYPES THE WHOLE DIVISION SHARES. The core's `Party` has no foreign company and no authorised representative,
-- so this module declares its own (and NEEDS-CORE.md records the constructors the core lacks).

§ `Who a rule of Division 2 is about`

-- The party of a regulative rule of Division 2: the foreign company, one of its directors, one of its authorised
-- representatives, one of its officers. Each carries a name; the regulative rules take it as an input.
DECLARE `s 365 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 365 the foreign company` HAS `s 365 the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING
    `s 365 a director of the foreign company` HAS `s 365 the name of the director` IS A STRING
    `s 365 an authorised representative of the foreign company` HAS `s 365 the name of the authorised representative` IS A STRING
    `s 365 an officer of the foreign company` HAS `s 365 the name of the officer` IS A STRING

-- The role a person has in an offence provision of Division 2 (s 368A(5), s 372(1C), s 373(18), s 373(18A), s 378(7), s 386).
-- "Director" here includes the "equivalent person" the text names beside the director in s 373(18) and (18A).
DECLARE `s 365 role` IS ONE OF
    `s 365 role: the foreign company`
    `s 365 role: a director of the foreign company, or an equivalent person`
    `s 365 role: an authorised representative of the foreign company`
    `s 365 role: an officer of the foreign company`
    `s 365 role: someone else`

§ `Section 365: foreign companies to which this Division applies`

-- src:23613 | Foreign companies to which this Division applies
-- src:23615 | 365. This Division applies to a foreign company which —
-- src:23616 | (a) establishes a place of business or carries on business in
-- src:23617 | Singapore; or
-- src:23622 | (b) intends to establish a place of business or carry on business
-- src:23623 | in Singapore.
@ref s 365 (src:23613-23623)
GIVEN body IS A `s 4(1) body`
      `the foreign company establishes a place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company carries on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign company intends to establish a place of business or carry on business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 365 this Division applies to the foreign company` MEANS
    IF    `s 4(1) "foreign company" the body is a foreign company` body EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (    `the foreign company establishes a place of business in Singapore`
             OR `the foreign company carries on business in Singapore`
             OR `the foreign company intends to establish a place of business or carry on business in Singapore`)
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a) establishes a place of business or carries on business in Singapore; or (b) intends to establish a place of business or carry on business in Singapore
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Division applies to a foreign company which" names the companies it applies to, without "only", so a body that is not a foreign company, or one that does none of (a) and (b), is outside the scope: the scope-limit ruling (c) of 2026-11-05

§ `Section 366(1): "authorised representative" and "carrying on business"`

-- src:23627 | Interpretation of this Division
-- src:23629 | 366.—(1) In this Division, unless the contrary intention appears —
-- src:23631 | “authorised representative”, in relation to a foreign company,
-- src:23632 | means —
-- src:23634 | (a) in the case of a foreign company registered before
-- src:23635 | 3 January 2016 — the agent of the foreign company
-- src:23636 | as defined by this section in force immediately before
-- src:23637 | that date; and
-- src:23639 | (b) in the case of a foreign company registered on or after
-- src:23640 | 3 January 2016 — the person named in a notice
-- src:23641 | lodged under section 368(1)(e);
@ref s 366(1) "authorised representative" (src:23627-23641)
GIVEN `the day the foreign company was registered` IS A DATE
      `the person was the agent of the foreign company as defined by section 366 in force immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is named in a notice lodged under section 368(1)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 366(1) "authorised representative" the person is an authorised representative of the foreign company` MEANS
    IF `the day the foreign company was registered` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
    THEN (IF `the person was the agent of the foreign company as defined by section 366 in force immediately before 3 January 2016`
          THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a) registered before 3 January 2016: the agent as the section defined it before that date
          ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“authorised representative”, in relation to a foreign company, means — (a) in the case of a foreign company registered before 3 January 2016 — the agent of the foreign company as defined by this section in force immediately before that date" (a "means" definition)
    ELSE (IF `the person is named in a notice lodged under section 368(1)(e)`
          THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b) registered on or after 3 January 2016: the person named in a notice lodged under section 368(1)(e)
          ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the case of a foreign company registered on or after 3 January 2016 — the person named in a notice lodged under section 368(1)(e)" (a "means" definition)

-- "carrying on business": (a) "includes" administration, management or other dealing with property in Singapore as agent, legal personal
-- representative or trustee; (b) "does not exclude" activities carried on without a view to profit.
-- src:23643 | “carrying on business” —
-- src:23645 | (a) includes the administration, management or
-- src:23646 | otherwise dealing with property situated in
-- src:23647 | Singapore as an agent, a legal personal
-- src:23648 | representative, or a trustee, whether by employees
-- src:23649 | or agents or otherwise; and
-- src:23651 | (b) does not exclude activities carried on without a view
-- src:23652 | to any profit.
@ref s 366(1) "carrying on business" (src:23643-23652)
GIVEN `the activity is the administration, management or otherwise dealing with property situated in Singapore as an agent, a legal personal representative, or a trustee, whether by employees or agents or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 366(1) "carrying on business" the activity is within carrying on business` MEANS
    IF `the activity is the administration, management or otherwise dealing with property situated in Singapore as an agent, a legal personal representative, or a trustee, whether by employees or agents or otherwise`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a) "includes the administration, management or otherwise dealing with property situated in Singapore as an agent, a legal personal representative, or a trustee"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“carrying on business” — (a) includes ..." leaves the list open

@ref s 366(1) "carrying on business" (src:23651-23652)
GIVEN `the activity is carried on without a view to any profit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 366(1) "carrying on business" the activity is kept out of carrying on business only because it is carried on without a view to any profit` MEANS
    IF `the activity is carried on without a view to any profit`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“carrying on business” — ... (b) does not exclude activities carried on without a view to any profit" (a flat negative: the absence of a profit motive is not a ground for exclusion; it does not say the activity is carrying on business)
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph speaks only of activities without a view to profit

§ `Section 366(2): what a foreign company is not regarded as doing by reason only of an activity`

DECLARE `s 366(2) activity` IS ONE OF
    `s 366(2)(a) being or becoming a party to an action, suit, administrative or arbitration proceeding, or effecting a settlement of one, or of a claim or dispute`
    `s 366(2)(b) holding meetings of its directors or shareholders, or carrying on other activities concerning its internal affairs`
    `s 366(2)(c) maintaining a bank account`
    `s 366(2)(d) effecting a sale through an independent contractor`
    `s 366(2)(e) soliciting or procuring an order that becomes a binding contract only if accepted outside Singapore`
    `s 366(2)(f) creating evidence of a debt, or creating a charge on movable or immovable property`
    `s 366(2)(g) securing or collecting its debts, or enforcing its rights in regard to securities relating to such debts`
    `s 366(2)(h) conducting an isolated transaction`
    `s 366(2)(i) investing any of its funds or holding any property`
    `s 366(2)(j) establishing a share transfer or share registration office in Singapore`
    `s 366(2)(k) effecting a transaction through its related corporation`
    `s 366(2)(l) carrying on an activity the Minister has prescribed`
    `s 366(2) some other activity`

-- src:23656 | (2) Despite subsection (1), a foreign company is not to be regarded
-- src:23657 | as carrying on business in Singapore for the reason only that in
-- src:23658 | Singapore it —
-- src:23660 | (a) is or becomes a party to any action or suit or any
-- src:23661 | administrative or arbitration proceeding or effects
-- src:23662 | settlement of an action, suit or proceeding or of any
-- src:23663 | claim or dispute;
-- src:23665 | (b) holds meetings of its directors or shareholders or carries on
-- src:23666 | other activities concerning its internal affairs;
-- src:23668 | (c) maintains any bank account;
-- src:23673 | (d) effects any sale through an independent contractor;
-- src:23675 | (e) solicits or procures any order which becomes a binding
-- src:23676 | contract only if such order is accepted outside Singapore;
-- src:23678 | (f) creates evidence of any debt or creates a charge on
-- src:23679 | movable or immovable property;
-- src:23681 | (g) secures or collects any of its debts or enforces its rights in
-- src:23682 | regard to any securities relating to such debts;
-- src:23684 | (h) conducts an isolated transaction that is completed within a
-- src:23685 | period of 31 days, but not being one of a number of similar
-- src:23686 | transactions repeated from time to time;
-- src:23688 | (i) invests any of its funds or holds any property;
-- src:23690 | (j) establishes a share transfer or share registration office in
-- src:23691 | Singapore;
-- src:23693 | (k) effects any transaction through its related corporation
-- src:23694 | licensed or approved under any written law by the
-- src:23695 | Monetary Authority of Singapore, established under the
-- src:23696 | Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970, under an
-- src:23697 | arrangement approved by the Monetary Authority of
-- src:23698 | Singapore; or
-- src:23700 | (l) carries on such other activity as the Minister may
-- src:23701 | prescribe.
@ref s 366(2) (src:23656-23701)
GIVEN `the activity` IS A `s 366(2) activity`
      `the number of days in which the isolated transaction was completed` IS A NUMBER
      `the isolated transaction is one of a number of similar transactions repeated from time to time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the related corporation is licensed or approved under a written law by the Monetary Authority of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is effected under an arrangement approved by the Monetary Authority of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has prescribed the activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 366(2) the foreign company is not regarded as carrying on business in Singapore by reason only of the activity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `s 366(2)(a) being or becoming a party to an action, suit, administrative or arbitration proceeding, or effecting a settlement of one, or of a claim or dispute` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 366(2)(b) holding meetings of its directors or shareholders, or carrying on other activities concerning its internal affairs` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 366(2)(c) maintaining a bank account` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 366(2)(d) effecting a sale through an independent contractor` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 366(2)(e) soliciting or procuring an order that becomes a binding contract only if accepted outside Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 366(2)(f) creating evidence of a debt, or creating a charge on movable or immovable property` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 366(2)(g) securing or collecting its debts, or enforcing its rights in regard to securities relating to such debts` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 366(2)(h) conducting an isolated transaction` THEN
        (IF `the number of days in which the isolated transaction was completed` AT MOST 31 AND (NOT `the isolated transaction is one of a number of similar transactions repeated from time to time`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(h) conducts an isolated transaction that is completed within a period of 31 days, but not being one of a number of similar transactions repeated from time to time": a transaction that took longer, or is one of a repeated series, is outside the paragraph, and the paragraph says nothing of it
    WHEN `s 366(2)(i) investing any of its funds or holding any property` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 366(2)(j) establishing a share transfer or share registration office in Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 366(2)(k) effecting a transaction through its related corporation` THEN
        (IF `the related corporation is licensed or approved under a written law by the Monetary Authority of Singapore` AND `the transaction is effected under an arrangement approved by the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(k) effects any transaction through its related corporation licensed or approved under any written law by the Monetary Authority of Singapore ... under an arrangement approved by the Monetary Authority of Singapore"
    WHEN `s 366(2)(l) carrying on an activity the Minister has prescribed` THEN
        (IF `the Minister has prescribed the activity`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "(l) carries on such other activity as the Minister may prescribe": what the Minister prescribes is not among the sources
    WHEN `s 366(2) some other activity` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraphs name twelve activities and do not say "only"; an activity outside them is not covered by this subsection

§ `Section 367: power to hold immovable property`

-- src:23707 | 367. Subject to and in accordance with any written law, a foreign
-- src:23708 | company registered under this Division has power to hold immovable
-- src:23709 | property in Singapore.
@ref s 367 (src:23707-23709)
GIVEN `the foreign company is registered under this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holding is in accordance with the written law that governs it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 367 the foreign company has power to hold immovable property in Singapore` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company is registered under this Division` AND `the holding is in accordance with the written law that governs it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to and in accordance with any written law, a foreign company registered under this Division has power to hold immovable property in Singapore": a grant of a power; where the company is not registered, or the holding is not in accordance with the written law, the text does not say the company lacks the power (the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1)
